#Strategy Advisor
("sod_sa_in_castle_1", "My rule of soldiers is simple: judge them by what they survive, not by the shine on their gear. Recruits learn fear, backbone troops learn work, veterans learn timing, elites learn command, and legends make the enemy remember their names."),
("sod_sa_in_castle_2", "You prevailed. Good. Now comes the uglier craft: holding roads, feeding garrisons, and teaching neighbors that your banners are not passing weather."),
("sod_sa_in_castle_3", "Ask the Chancellor about surviving homeland lords when you can support them. Some lost everything to the Legion. Give them land, purpose, and proof that your court is not merely another exile's dream."),
("sod_sa_in_castle_4", "Faith buildings are not only stone and prayer. They tell frightened people that your rule has a memory longer than the next raid."),
("sod_sa_in_castle_5", "Upgrade troops in batches when you can arm and station them properly. A hundred men learning together become a regiment. A hundred scattered promotions become a wage bill with boots."),
("sod_sa_in_castle_6", "The engineers are not wrong about hand cannons. I dislike the smell, the smoke, and the politics of them, which usually means they are about to change warfare."),
("sod_sa_in_castle_7", "Once you claim a castle or town, ask your Chancellor what land and administration you need before inviting lords. Noble loyalty begins with poetry and ends with acreage."),
("sod_sa_in_castle_8", "When you declare your own kingdom, village recruits become raw peasants until your Marshal shapes them. Buildings decide the training path; neglect decides the casualty list."),
("sod_sa_in_castle_9", "Automatic garrisons are useful, but every soldier in a wall is also food, wages, and a missing hand in the fields. Defense without population becomes a siege you perform on yourself."),
("sod_sa_in_castle_10", "The Jester beat me at chess three times before I found the extra piece in his sleeve. I let him keep the story. A court needs laughter, provided it does not command the army."),

